PLAIN WORDS (patch ignores this header; apply from the kit folder with:  patch -p1 < this file)
FIX 1 of the three kit blockers: the Astra roof sets its materials INSIDE a geometry-nodes modifier and carries its tiles on a hidden object that is not in the scene,
so the role finder never saw them and no layer (moss, dust film) could reach the roof. describe_scene() now also lists the materials of the EVALUATED scene
(what the modifier sets, what its instances carry), credited to the scene object that owns them, and puts them AFTER the object's own slot materials.
TESTED (21 Oct, Blender 5.2.2, headless): role maps of the street and the lockout file are byte-for-byte unchanged; on the courtyard 'Hall roof' gains the three roof materials
(role roof.tile) and soot and wallgrowth now go into them (5 -> 8 and 102 -> 105 materials). Attribute nodes (type Object) read the OWNING object's custom properties for
instances, in Cycles and EEVEE alike (tested), so no per-object values had to change.
NOT TESTED: a picture with the roof mossed (the small EEVEE preview timed out at 200 s on this computer's software graphics).

